00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.709
During my Ph.D, which resulted in

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:33.819
the book, the Romanian Orthodox

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.079
Church and the Holocaust, published

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.899
by Indiana University Press in 2017,

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:39.609
I discovered that in relation to the

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:41.589
topic of Jewish conversion,

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:43.599
the main church in Romania

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.239
had to address two issues.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.099
First, there were requests

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.809
from Jews who were already converted

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:51.490
to Orthodox Christianity to

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.189
be protected by the religion they

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:56.909
have been members of for many years.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.269
Unfortunately, the Holy Synod

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.159
refused to offer any help,

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.229
not even to those such as Nicolae

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:03.230
Solamonescu,

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.919
a Jewish man who converted more than

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:07.989
thirty years before.

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:09.609
Second, there were requests for

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.529
baptism during the Holocaust coming

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.449
from Jews who believe that in this

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:15.519
way they may be protected by

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:17.289
the increasing anti-Semitic laws.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:20.229
In the second instance, the Romanian

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:21.789
Orthodox Church showed indifference

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:22.790
too.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:25.239
Although it had a clear majority

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:26.799
of at least 72 percent of the

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.719
population, the church offered

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:30.639
this avenue to only a

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:32.559
handful of people, this being

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.509
in stark contrast with the attitude

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:36.279
of the Roman Catholic, Greek

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:38.080
Catholic and Lutheran churches.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.049
When I finished my Ph.D., I embarked

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:45.029
on a new project looking at the big

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.739
discrepancy between the attitude of

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:47.819
the Orthodox and the Catholic

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:50.009
churches in Romania toward Jews.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:51.929
Although the topic of

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.789
conversion was not the only one I

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.589
looked at, it was one of the most

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.089
important as the Catholic Church in

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:59.009
Romania made it a matter of open

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:00.479
rebellion against the state.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:01.769
And by the way, this is the Papal

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:03.629
nuncio to Bucharest,

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:04.630
Andrea Cassulo.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:07.979
In Romania, there are two

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.779
strands of Catholicism, Greek

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:10.780
Catholicism,

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.609
which comprise of

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:16.859
ethnic Romanians from Transylvania,

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.059
who at the beginning of the 18th

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.979
century accepted to be subjected

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.929
to the Holy See, and the regular

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:23.639
Roman Catholics.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:25.799
Both Catholic churches

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:27.299
were in struggle with the Romanian

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.189
state, which favored the Romanian

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:30.389
Orthodox Church.

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.429
Hence, in 1941,

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:34.679
when the Antonescu regime

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.209
banned conversion of Jews, the

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.039
Catholic Church protested vehemently

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.239
against the measure.

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.489
In the coming years, many Jews

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:43.319
who understood that conversion to

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:44.699
Catholicism might offer some

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:47.759
protection asked to be baptized.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.679
The Catholics seized the opportunity

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.599
to show their defiance and continue

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.119
to convert in open disobedience,

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.129
sometimes resisting direct pressures

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:58.769
from the state to stop baptism.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:00.929
As the Antonescu regime wanted

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:02.369
to maintain good relations with the

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.959
Vatican, which was seen by the

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:06.029
Romanian leader as a key political

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:07.319
player in the future peace

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.149
conferences, most youth who

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:10.559
converted to Catholicism during the

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.299
Holocaust in Romania escaped

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:14.399
deportation and death.

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.619
Lists found in various archives

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.989
show that at least 2,008

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:21.779
Jews converted after the March 1941.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:22.780
ban.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:05:24.569
These should be added to the

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:27.539
4,631 Jews who were

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:28.740
already converts.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.869
During my research, I was surprised

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.399
by the lack of information on the

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:37.259
postwar fate of converted

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:38.279
Jews.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:39.749
I remember that when I started my

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:41.199
postdoctoral project, I discovered

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.199
at Yad Vashem lists of Jews

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:44.549
who converted to Catholicism in

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:45.550
Bukovina.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.519
I took one of these lists which

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:49.889
comprised of 108 names,

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:51.659
and tried to find any information in

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.309
the Yad Vashem Hall of Names, and

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:55.289
other paper and video

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.059
archives at Yad Vashem.

00:05:57.060 --> 00:05:58.709
At the time. I also introduced the

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:00.320
names in the USH, USC

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:03.359
Shoah Foundation video archive.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.519
Unfortunately, I found nothing.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.379
I even arranged a meeting with the

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:08.759
director of the Hall of Names, who

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.049
explained to me that since they

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:11.669
converted, it must be that these

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:13.799
people either did not identify

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.079
as Jews, or were not accepted

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.660
or seen as Jews anymore.

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:21.089
In 1950s, the case

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:22.670
of Daniel Ruf, Rufeison,

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:26.099
showed that the convert's Jewishness

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.949
was strongly contested in Israel.

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:31.089
Historian and sociologist Ariel

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.069
Yaakov, mentions--

00:06:33.070 --> 00:06:35.319
sorry, mentions

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:36.939
in one of his articles several

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:38.379
memoirs of Holocaust survivors that

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:40.239
discuss openly the topic of

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.609
conversion, and it is striking that

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:44.259
all of them were written and

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:45.790
published in the United States.

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:49.299
In the US, the topic of conversion

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.009
appears more often in testimonies of

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.509
Holocaust survivors, including in

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:54.099
the Fortunoff Archive.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:55.479
There are several aspects that might

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:56.289
explain this.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.299
First, it is already generally

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:00.519
accepted that the American identity

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.439
is based on multiple ethnic and

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.999
religious layers.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.889
Hence, one does not feel the need

00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:08.529
to define himself or herself

00:07:08.530 --> 00:07:10.209
in limited ethnic and religious

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:11.019
terms.

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:12.549
Second, the Jewish community in the

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:15.129
United States is much more eclectic

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:17.019
and the definition of Jewishness is

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:18.879
more nuanced than in Europe or

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:20.289
Israel.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:21.879
This might explain why a Jewish

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:23.739
convert to Christianity could talk

00:07:23.740 --> 00:07:25.569
openly about conversion, conversion

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.399
and still identify as Jewish

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.379
in the US, but would have

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:30.879
reservations to do so in other

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:32.229
countries.

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:33.489
Third, since the definition of

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:35.349
Jewishness is broader and more

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:37.389
inclusive, some US, US

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.039
institutions that gather Holocaust

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:40.929
survivors' testimonies did not

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.399
have any problem of including

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.019
testimonies of Jews who converted to

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.020
Christianity.

00:07:47.710 --> 00:07:48.819
This was definitely the case with

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:50.229
the Fortunoff Video Archive.

00:07:50.230 --> 00:07:51.789
The project to gather testimonies of

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:54.369
Holocaust survivors started in 1979,

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.779
and I argue that from the beginning

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:57.279
it is visible the broader scope and

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:58.599
reach of the project.

00:07:58.600 --> 00:08:00.069
Take, for example, one of the first

00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:02.079
interviews done by Lauren

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.999
Vlock, Laurel Vlock, one of the

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:06.099
initiators of the archive in 1980,

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:07.929
April 1980

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:09.789
with Hans Frei, who was at the

00:08:09.790 --> 00:08:11.199
time a respected professor of

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:12.849
theology at the Yale Divinity

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:13.850
School.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.559
Frei was born in Breslau

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:18.449
in 1922,

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:20.159
from Jewish parents were both

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:21.740
involved in the medical profession.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:24.149
His father was a professor at the

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:25.559
Faculty of Medicine, University of

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.389
Breslau, and his mother was a

00:08:27.390 --> 00:08:28.469
doctor.

00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:30.029
The parents were much assimilated

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.289
into the German society.

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:32.759
They converted to Christianity in

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:34.408
their early adulthood.

00:08:34.409 --> 00:08:36.298
In 1935, Hans was

00:08:36.299 --> 00:08:38.369
sent to a Quaker school

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.229
in England as a way of protecting

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:42.979
him from increasing persecution.

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:45.079
In 1938, the entire

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:46.519
family immigrated to the United

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:47.520
States.

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:49.749
The problem of conversion and the

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:51.789
definition of one's belongings,

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:53.649
belonging is in depth debated

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:55.359
in the dialog between Vlock and

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:57.249
Frei, and although I have

00:08:57.250 --> 00:08:58.779
not found yet a written document to

00:08:58.780 --> 00:09:00.519
confirm this, it might be that this

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.319
early interview set up later

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:04.449
practice of interviewing converts

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:06.369
and discussing the way in which

00:09:06.370 --> 00:09:08.589
the experience impacted

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:10.149
their sense of belonging.

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:14.759
The Fortunoff Video Archive

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:16.589
contains, in comparison to all

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:18.599
other Holocaust testimonies

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.459
archives I looked at,

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:22.229
a much greater number of testimonies

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:23.309
from Jews who converted to

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:24.809
Christianity before and during the

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:26.459
Second World War.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:27.899
I relied in my findings

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:31.739
on Orbis, the search

00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:34.169
engine of the Yale Library.

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.909
Each testimony has a brief, usually

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:38.019
between 10-20 lines,

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:39.969
rows in a word document,

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:42.329
this description of its content.

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:44.949
This tool is by no means perfect,

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:47.009
and there might be

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:48.459
other testimonies describing

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:50.489
experience of conversion that sees

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:52.409
the word itself or alternate

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:54.269
version, versions

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:55.919
are not mentioned in the description

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:57.179
are impossible to find.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:00.069
Using Orbis, I deployed

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:02.139
four types of search.

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:04.089
First, I searched using

00:10:04.090 --> 00:10:06.489
the word conversion and 63

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:08.049
results came up.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:10.929
Of the 63, 48

00:10:10.930 --> 00:10:12.819
turned out to be describing, some of

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:15.339
them in great detail, experiences

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:17.409
of conversion to Christianity.

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:19.479
In terms of gender, 28

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:21.369
testimonies were given by women

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:22.779
and 20 by men.

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:25.799
The vast majority were children

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:27.359
at the moment of conversion, being

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.399
born in the late 1920s

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:31.409
and during the 1930s,

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:33.299
only few being born before

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:35.069
1920.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:37.019
Most conversions took place from

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:39.719
1939 to 1944.

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:41.729
Only three took place after

00:10:41.730 --> 00:10:44.099
the war and a few others before

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.009
1939.

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:47.479
The most striking aspect was the

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:48.589
distribution according to the

00:10:48.590 --> 00:10:50.419
country of origin, which was in

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:52.239
most cases, but not all,

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:53.209
also the country where the

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:55.849
experience of conversion took place.

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:57.379
The preponderance of testimonies

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:59.419
from Slovakia is surprising

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:00.754
and difficult to explain,

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:03.659
as it appears in the testimonies

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:05.549
themselves, conversion in itself

00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:07.499
was not providing safe shelter

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:08.969
in Slovakia.

00:11:08.970 --> 00:11:10.859
So this could not explain the large

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:12.479
number of testimonies and maybe of

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.519
conversions in this country.

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:16.379
The possibility that there was,

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:18.749
there was, is a Slovak community

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:20.909
around New Haven, hence more people

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:22.109
were interviewed as a result of

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.759
geographical proximity is not

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.799
entirely explanatory as testimonies

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:27.419
of the Fortunoff Archive were

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:29.429
gathered in many other

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:30.749
locations.

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:32.579
Another striking aspect was the fact

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.049
that there is no testimony from

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:36.039
Romania, including

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:37.299
territories that were part of

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.799
greater Romania in the interwar

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:40.779
period and are now in Ukraine

00:11:40.780 --> 00:11:43.779
or Moldova, the country

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:45.369
with the third largest Jewish

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:46.559
community before the war.

00:11:48.050 --> 00:11:49.669
Moreover, I explained about, as

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:51.469
explained above, the number of

00:11:51.470 --> 00:11:52.789
conversions in Romania during the

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:54.649
Holocaust was relatively, relatively

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:55.669
high.

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:57.739
The absence of any testimonies

00:11:57.740 --> 00:11:59.719
from this country could be a strong

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:01.739
argument of the way in which

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:03.859
effectiveness of conversion

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:06.589
affected postwar Jewish identity

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:07.969
and I hope we will be able to

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:09.439
discuss these more in the Q&amp;A

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:10.440
session.

00:12:11.510 --> 00:12:13.159
After the analysis of the first

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:14.959
sixty three testimonies resulted

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:17.059
from searching the word conversion,

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:19.009
I looked up for three more

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:21.109
variants, converted, baptism,

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:22.159
and baptized.

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:25.390
For the sake of

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:29.379
time, I will keep some details

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:30.999
about those findings that I will

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.219
offer an overall summary.

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:35.039
The four searches produced

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:37.449
one hundred and fifty three results.

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:39.189
Ninety seven out of a hundred and

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:40.479
fifty three were testimonies

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:42.099
describing in a form or another

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:43.689
experiences of conversion of the

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:45.519
interviewees, while

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:47.619
the rest were either duplicates

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:49.669
or irrelevant as the word refer

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:50.619
to something else.

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.479
Were, all were about

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:54.129
conversions of somebody else,

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:55.389
usually parents.

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:56.980
And the mention was very brief.

00:12:59.490 --> 00:13:01.199
Sixty two testimonies were from

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:03.329
women Holocaust survivors

00:13:03.330 --> 00:13:05.010
and 36 from men.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:07.749
The vast majority were children at

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.849
the time of baptism, conversion

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:11.889
to Catholicism is predominant,

00:13:11.890 --> 00:13:13.329
but this was mostly because most

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:14.559
testimonies were from countries

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:15.819
where Catholicism was the main

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:17.289
religion.

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:18.879
In terms of countries of origin, it

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:20.289
surprises the large number of

00:13:20.290 --> 00:13:22.869
testimonies from Slovakia, 26.

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:24.339
This is more than a quarter.

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:27.179
And the lack of any testimony from

00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:28.180
Romania.

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:30.839
In almost all cases looked at,

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:33.209
conversion was a means of survival.

00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:34.679
It was not the only strategy of

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:36.869
survival and most of that in itself

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:39.359
was not helpful or enough,

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:41.309
but it was always combined with

00:13:41.310 --> 00:13:43.259
other means of survival, such as

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:46.079
hiding or providing forged papers.

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:47.429
In some cases, some means of

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:49.619
survival were diffused without

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:50.850
the step of conversion.

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:54.659
Several historians have noted

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:56.069
that until today, the topic of

00:13:56.070 --> 00:13:57.539
conversion has been to a large

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.099
extent avoided in Holocaust

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:01.199
historiography, but conversion

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:02.579
was not a marginal aspect of the

00:14:02.580 --> 00:14:03.719
Holocaust.

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:05.099
On the one hand, as in the case of

00:14:05.100 --> 00:14:06.359
the Romanian Orthodox Church

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.279
explained earlier, judges

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:09.869
had to respond to Jews who were

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:11.190
already converts.

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:15.599
And I think it is stunning

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:16.949
that the topic is not carefully

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:18.539
discussed when one considers that in

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:21.029
Hungary alone in 1941,

00:14:21.030 --> 00:14:23.519
there were up to 100,000 converts.

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:25.649
That is approximately one sixth

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:28.019
of the Jewish population of Hungary.

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:29.339
This, including the territories,

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:32.859
added, added, annexed after 1940.

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:34.269
Although there were converts

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:36.009
deported to Auschwitz and there are

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:37.299
few such testimonies in the

00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:39.369
Fortunoff Archive, most

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:41.439
of them were protected as in 1944,

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:43.029
Catholic and Protestant churches

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:44.769
protested vehemently the deportation

00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:46.329
of converts.

00:14:46.330 --> 00:14:47.979
The number of converts, what, was

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:50.049
high in other countries, too.

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:51.789
In Russia, for example, during the

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:53.469
19th century, the official number of

00:14:53.470 --> 00:14:55.299
conversion was 85,000.

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:57.939
Czechoslovakia, although we lack

00:14:57.940 --> 00:15:00.039
clear figures, it is estimated

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.080
that in Prague or Brno

00:15:04.030 --> 00:15:05.139
at the beginning of the 20th

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:06.669
century, the conversion rate stood

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:07.670
at 2.25

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:10.929
or 2.5 percent of the local Jewish

00:15:10.930 --> 00:15:11.930
population.

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:14.719
Hans Frei puts the number

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:17.119
of converts in Germany in 1933

00:15:17.120 --> 00:15:18.120
at 15,000.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:21.439
On the other hand, churches had to

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.729
deal during the Holocaust with

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:24.979
another aspect: to convert

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:27.529
and if so, under what circumstances,

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:30.229
Jews who are seeking protection.

00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:31.579
The case of Romania, where the

00:15:31.580 --> 00:15:33.379
Catholic Church converted entire

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:35.179
families in open disobedience to

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:37.099
state, state pressures, is

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:38.689
singular.

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:40.369
In other countries, conversion was

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:42.949
not necessarily an official policy

00:15:42.950 --> 00:15:44.239
coming from the leadership of the

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:45.559
church, but a matter of local

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:47.899
initiative and decision.

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:49.579
For example, there were cases of

00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:51.199
Jews who wanted to take shelter in a

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.539
village, but the villagers said

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:55.279
that they would not offer that

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:57.139
protection unless the Jews

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:58.659
convert to Catholicism.

00:16:01.300 --> 00:16:02.860
This situation appears

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:06.039
several times in the Fortunoff

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:07.909
testimony that I mentioned here,

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:08.949
only the case of Ann W.,

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:11.210
Holocaust testimony

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:15.069
2356. Was from a town

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.070
called Radzilow

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:17.859
in Poland.

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:19.779
She described the scene when her

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:21.039
father asked the leader of the

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.049
village to help the family.

00:16:23.050 --> 00:16:24.849
Quote, "he asked him if he could

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:25.959
help us.

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:27.669
There were some other people and the

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.679
first comment that there

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:31.629
was from those people was,

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:34.059
'as Jews, we cannot help you.

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:36.339
If you promise to convert,

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:38.289
then we will try and help you.'

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:40.269
Of course, my father agreed." End

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:41.270
of quote.

00:16:41.590 --> 00:16:43.419
And since I mentioned on here,

00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:45.409
I must stress an aspect that

00:16:45.410 --> 00:16:47.499
she mentioned, mentions and

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:49.359
is not very often present in

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:50.319
testimonies.

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:52.029
The role of the parents in this

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:53.799
case, the parents and children, were

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:55.959
hiding together in keeping

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:57.849
alive Jewish identity despite

00:16:57.850 --> 00:16:59.169
conversion.

00:16:59.170 --> 00:17:00.969
And I have the clip actually from...

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:10.550
Uh

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:15.010
uh.

00:17:15.849 --> 00:17:17.460
Would uh, would talk to me.

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:20.828
All the talk was, was this

00:17:20.829 --> 00:17:21.669
because--

00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:22.730
My mother, my mother would talk,

00:17:22.731 --> 00:17:23.731
--heard.

00:17:26.050 --> 00:17:28.118
She would talk to me, she would,

00:17:28.119 --> 00:17:29.769
being that I was the youngest and I

00:17:29.770 --> 00:17:31.090
didn't have much education yet.

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:34.599
She, she would tell me about the

00:17:34.600 --> 00:17:36.579
Jewish history

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:38.079
and heritage.

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:39.969
And, eh, she wanted to be sure that

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:42.069
I know who I am, and

00:17:42.070 --> 00:17:44.199
the, and who my people

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:46.149
are. And she tried

00:17:46.150 --> 00:17:48.009
to instill in me the

00:17:48.010 --> 00:17:50.319
pride of being Jewish

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:52.299
and not to think that because we

00:17:52.300 --> 00:17:53.300
are exterminated

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:56.269
and eh, and treated the way

00:17:56.270 --> 00:17:58.209
we are, that we really deserve

00:17:58.210 --> 00:17:59.319
that.

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:01.239
And they, and

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:02.240
she would tell me

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:05.589
stories with the history about

00:18:05.590 --> 00:18:08.049
some heroic, especially

00:18:08.050 --> 00:18:10.299
heroic events that took place.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:13.599
And she would tell me that if,

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:15.879
in case I'm the only one

00:18:15.880 --> 00:18:17.769
who would survive, to be

00:18:17.770 --> 00:18:19.659
sure to somehow get

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:21.519
through a, to a center where there

00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:23.529
are Jews and the,

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:26.499
and to, to go to Palestine

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:29.179
and, and go on with my life

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:30.180
and,

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:33.039
and that, that there is

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:35.229
so much beauty

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:37.089
in, in the way of life of

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:39.329
Jews in their daily living.

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:43.629
The re-telling of the story with

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:45.609
this heroic undertones

00:18:45.610 --> 00:18:47.049
was definitely influenced by the

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:48.969
interviewee's situation,

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:50.799
belief values, as they were

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:52.689
in the 1980s when the interview

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:53.559
was done.

00:18:53.560 --> 00:18:56.769
Still, the scene itself shows

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:58.779
the desire of parents to pass on

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.639
to their children their,

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:02.979
their ethnic and religious identity

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:05.109
in a context in which they were in,

00:19:05.110 --> 00:19:06.210
that to some extent, foggy.

00:19:07.980 --> 00:19:09.959
We should not forget that they were

00:19:11.790 --> 00:19:13.859
converted already, hiding,

00:19:13.860 --> 00:19:14.939
but they are still trying to

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:16.569
maintain a Jewish identity alive.

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:18.959
Other parents do not have this

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:21.509
chance during the Holocaust.

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:23.669
The conditioning of help in exchange

00:19:23.670 --> 00:19:25.439
for conversion appears often in

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:27.519
attitudes of religious institutions

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:28.319
too.

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:29.789
Many Catholic and Protestant

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:32.849
convents and/or orphanages

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:35.189
refuse to take children inside

00:19:35.190 --> 00:19:37.389
unless they converted.

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:39.479
For example, David K., Holocaust

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:40.619
testimony 1856,

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:43.160
who was born in Brno,

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:46.109
explains that an Anglican orphanage

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:47.110
based in Czechoslovakia

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:49.739
conditioned the acceptance of the

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:51.690
Jewish children on their baptism.

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:54.409
While hiding in convents or in

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:56.449
Catholic households, many

00:19:56.450 --> 00:19:58.099
Jewish children felt persuaded to

00:19:58.100 --> 00:20:00.259
convert. Sometimes there were

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:02.289
direct pressures.

00:20:02.290 --> 00:20:04.279
Other times there was a

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:05.749
winning over.

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:07.579
Such examples--

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:10.099
we know of the child being convinced

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:12.079
by the context in which he or she

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:13.489
was living.

00:20:13.490 --> 00:20:15.169
And there are many such examples in

00:20:15.170 --> 00:20:18.259
the Fortunoff testimonies archive.

00:20:18.260 --> 00:20:19.579
All these experiences impacted

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:21.409
greatly on these peoples later sense

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:22.410
of belonging.

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:24.769
On the one hand, there was an

00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:26.899
internal voice of consciousness

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:28.459
telling them, especially if they

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:30.199
grew in traditional Jewish families,

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:32.059
that by converting they betrayed the

00:20:32.060 --> 00:20:33.889
Jewish people, the Jewish religion,

00:20:33.890 --> 00:20:34.890
and community.

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:40.049
Take, for example, Susan

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:41.707
M., Holocaust testimony

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:45.329
537, who almost

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:48.029
converted as a child in Hungary

00:20:48.030 --> 00:20:49.739
to avoid persecution.

00:20:49.740 --> 00:20:51.479
She describes her experience in

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:52.649
these terms.

00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:55.349
I quote, "and the issue was,"

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:56.249
this is the voice of the

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:58.109
interviewer. "And the issue was that

00:20:58.110 --> 00:20:59.249
you were learning the Catholic

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:01.139
prayers." "Yes." "And you

00:21:01.140 --> 00:21:03.119
enjoyed taking

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:04.739
some lessons where you were a good

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:07.349
student." "No,

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:08.999
I was petrified the whole time.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:10.859
And I wanted to cover my ears not to

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:11.849
even hear it.

00:21:11.850 --> 00:21:13.619
And I felt somehow that God was

00:21:13.620 --> 00:21:15.329
watching us. And if anything, this

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:17.279
was going to be the cause

00:21:17.280 --> 00:21:18.599
of our perishing,

00:21:20.070 --> 00:21:22.559
the next air raid or whatever,

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:24.859
just because we were doing it.

00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:26.689
It was like, like being

00:21:26.690 --> 00:21:28.669
a traitor, and I was always terribly

00:21:28.670 --> 00:21:29.670
ashamed.

00:21:30.230 --> 00:21:32.059
I don't, I

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:33.829
am not ashamed of anything else

00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:35.209
associated with the Holocaust and I

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:36.679
practically talk about anything

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:38.569
else. But this is something I've

00:21:38.570 --> 00:21:40.819
always been very embarrassed

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:42.919
about. And I was

00:21:42.920 --> 00:21:44.989
glad when my father kicked up

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:46.969
a fight and we got out of

00:21:46.970 --> 00:21:48.040
it." End of quote.

00:21:49.520 --> 00:21:51.919
Susan M. is only one example

00:21:51.920 --> 00:21:53.839
of many others who had the same

00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:55.889
feeling of betrayal.

00:21:55.890 --> 00:21:57.299
At this interview, the voice of

00:21:57.300 --> 00:21:59.189
consciousness, one should also

00:21:59.190 --> 00:22:01.049
add the outsider problem.

00:22:01.050 --> 00:22:02.799
In many Jewish communities, converts

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:04.739
who are not welcome back, not

00:22:04.740 --> 00:22:06.389
seen as Jews anymore.

00:22:06.390 --> 00:22:08.489
Sometimes this implicit pressure

00:22:08.490 --> 00:22:09.719
can be felt in the Fortunoff

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:11.399
testimonies when the survivors try

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:13.709
to answer and ask questions,

00:22:13.710 --> 00:22:15.089
minimize the importance of

00:22:15.090 --> 00:22:17.339
conversion experience,

00:22:17.340 --> 00:22:19.649
or all of a sudden

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:21.539
bring up Israel as a way of

00:22:21.540 --> 00:22:24.619
emphasizing their Jewish belonging.

00:22:24.620 --> 00:22:26.419
And I don't know if you noticed,

00:22:26.420 --> 00:22:28.459
noticed, even in Ann's case,

00:22:28.460 --> 00:22:30.409
she's talking towards the end about

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:31.410
go, going to Palestine.

00:22:32.910 --> 00:22:34.799
Although most Fortunoff testimonies,

00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:36.419
discussion, discussing the impact of

00:22:36.420 --> 00:22:38.069
conversion of Jewish identity have

00:22:38.070 --> 00:22:39.989
this tone, there are

00:22:39.990 --> 00:22:42.479
several notable exceptions.

00:22:42.480 --> 00:22:44.099
There were few conversions after the

00:22:44.100 --> 00:22:44.939
Holocaust.

00:22:44.940 --> 00:22:47.099
In one case that was designed

00:22:47.100 --> 00:22:48.719
as an explicit protest against

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:51.029
Jewish religion and God seen

00:22:51.030 --> 00:22:53.639
as responsible for what happened.

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:55.829
So, I found such a case

00:22:55.830 --> 00:22:57.179
of a conversion as a sign of

00:22:57.180 --> 00:22:58.180
protest.

00:22:59.150 --> 00:23:01.339
There were other cases such as

00:23:01.340 --> 00:23:03.409
Walter Ziffer,

00:23:03.410 --> 00:23:05.290
testimony 1475,

00:23:06.950 --> 00:23:08.659
who converted after the Holocaust

00:23:08.660 --> 00:23:10.999
and after arrival in the US

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:12.000
out of conviction.

00:23:12.980 --> 00:23:14.659
Zimpher became a prominent

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:16.759
evangelical minister.

00:23:16.760 --> 00:23:18.769
But even in his case, testimony,

00:23:18.770 --> 00:23:20.959
one has the sense of a heroic return

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:23.119
to Judaism after almost

00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:24.230
40 years.

00:23:25.820 --> 00:23:27.949
Then there are testimonies of Jews

00:23:27.950 --> 00:23:29.539
who converted before and during the

00:23:29.540 --> 00:23:31.429
Holocaust in Germany.

00:23:31.430 --> 00:23:33.289
In most cases, their

00:23:33.290 --> 00:23:35.119
retelling of the story of conversion

00:23:35.120 --> 00:23:37.009
is not shadowed by

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:38.329
feelings of betrayal or

00:23:38.330 --> 00:23:40.159
embarrassment, and

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:41.719
that is probably because this

00:23:41.720 --> 00:23:44.450
community was much secularized.

00:23:46.600 --> 00:23:48.064
This is the case of Hans Frei,

00:23:49.120 --> 00:23:50.859
whom I mentioned earlier.

00:23:50.860 --> 00:23:52.659
After long deliberations, I decided

00:23:52.660 --> 00:23:54.609
to focus my annotated edition on his

00:23:54.610 --> 00:23:56.049
testimony.

00:23:56.050 --> 00:23:57.939
Frei's testimony is important for

00:23:57.940 --> 00:23:59.769
Yale University as

00:23:59.770 --> 00:24:01.659
he was a professor

00:24:01.660 --> 00:24:03.489
of theology here, Divinity

00:24:03.490 --> 00:24:05.499
School, for many years.

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:07.239
I also believe that this is one of

00:24:07.240 --> 00:24:09.039
the first such testimonies from

00:24:09.040 --> 00:24:10.569
converted Jews recorded in the

00:24:10.570 --> 00:24:12.399
Fortunoff Archive and

00:24:12.400 --> 00:24:14.499
it set up later trends.

00:24:14.500 --> 00:24:16.599
The topic of conversions impact

00:24:16.600 --> 00:24:18.159
on Jewish identity is discussed

00:24:18.160 --> 00:24:19.869
brilIiantly in this testimony.

00:24:20.880 --> 00:24:22.709
However, this is also a

00:24:22.710 --> 00:24:24.569
very different case from most of

00:24:24.570 --> 00:24:25.859
the cases I looked at.

00:24:27.320 --> 00:24:29.239
Frei, first Frei

00:24:29.240 --> 00:24:31.099
immigrated with his entire family in

00:24:31.100 --> 00:24:32.689
1938.

00:24:32.690 --> 00:24:33.979
He experienced the beginning of the

00:24:33.980 --> 00:24:35.419
Holocaust in Germany but did not

00:24:35.420 --> 00:24:37.459
feel like most other

00:24:37.460 --> 00:24:39.229
survivors the full blow of

00:24:39.230 --> 00:24:40.609
persecution.

00:24:40.610 --> 00:24:42.349
Frei did not have to take shelter in

00:24:42.350 --> 00:24:44.749
a convent, or to

00:24:44.750 --> 00:24:46.369
be hidden conditionally by some

00:24:46.370 --> 00:24:48.289
villagers, or to convert

00:24:48.290 --> 00:24:49.789
as a way of gaining the trust of a

00:24:49.790 --> 00:24:52.339
convent or a foster family.

00:24:52.340 --> 00:24:54.139
However, his testimony is extremely

00:24:54.140 --> 00:24:55.399
relevant because it shows a

00:24:55.400 --> 00:24:57.559
different tone on conversion,

00:24:57.560 --> 00:24:59.839
where this decision is not dismissed

00:24:59.840 --> 00:25:01.609
as a betrayal or embarrassment, nor

00:25:01.610 --> 00:25:03.979
minimized under a glorious narrative

00:25:03.980 --> 00:25:06.619
of postwar return to Judaism.

00:25:06.620 --> 00:25:08.449
Frei try to make peace with these

00:25:08.450 --> 00:25:10.729
hybrid identities.

00:25:10.730 --> 00:25:13.189
He explains this rather neutral

00:25:13.190 --> 00:25:14.629
attitude in this way.

00:25:14.630 --> 00:25:17.059
And I have again the excerpt

00:25:17.060 --> 00:25:18.060
here.

00:25:23.350 --> 00:25:25.809
We had been so deeply assimulated,

00:25:25.810 --> 00:25:26.810
you see? So deeply assimulated

00:25:30.270 --> 00:25:32.379
that on the one hand, we were

00:25:32.380 --> 00:25:34.239
proud of the

00:25:34.240 --> 00:25:36.339
fact that we were Jewish

00:25:36.340 --> 00:25:38.248
in a curious, undefinable way.

00:25:39.910 --> 00:25:41.889
We felt that we were Jewish

00:25:41.890 --> 00:25:42.729
and that was that.

00:25:42.730 --> 00:25:43.900
Jews were good people.

00:25:45.010 --> 00:25:46.889
But on the other hand, we felt that

00:25:46.890 --> 00:25:48.999
it was simply a kind

00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:51.609
of cultural,

00:25:51.610 --> 00:25:53.799
religious distinctness,

00:25:53.800 --> 00:25:55.929
but not anything

00:25:55.930 --> 00:25:57.879
that interfered with our, first

00:25:57.880 --> 00:25:59.979
of all, being German citizens.

00:25:59.980 --> 00:26:01.659
You see our whole world--for just

00:26:01.660 --> 00:26:03.189
that reason, our whole world was

00:26:03.190 --> 00:26:04.190
turned far more upside down

00:26:05.440 --> 00:26:07.239
in 1933.

00:26:07.240 --> 00:26:09.039
We were robbed of our primary

00:26:09.040 --> 00:26:11.169
support. Namely our

00:26:11.170 --> 00:26:12.789
national identity,

00:26:14.440 --> 00:26:16.419
which was much more our identity

00:26:16.420 --> 00:26:17.740
than our Jewish identity.

00:26:18.850 --> 00:26:21.519
This is a complex story because

00:26:21.520 --> 00:26:23.109
you were converted.

00:26:23.110 --> 00:26:25.029
You claim you felt Jewish

00:26:25.030 --> 00:26:26.679
or you felt an identification with

00:26:26.680 --> 00:26:29.609
your Jewish heritage, ancestry,

00:26:29.610 --> 00:26:30.961
yet you were practicing Christians

00:26:32.500 --> 00:26:34.047
in an assimilated German society.

00:26:34.048 --> 00:26:35.048
It's, uh--

00:26:35.149 --> 00:26:36.149
Heinrich

00:26:37.090 --> 00:26:38.949
Heine, the German poet

00:26:38.950 --> 00:26:40.879
who was himself Jewish and

00:26:40.880 --> 00:26:42.969
rather cynically converted,

00:26:42.970 --> 00:26:44.829
once said that the-- that

00:26:44.830 --> 00:26:48.039
bap-- the baptismal certificate

00:26:48.040 --> 00:26:50.229
is the admission ticket to European

00:26:50.230 --> 00:26:51.230
culture.

00:26:52.330 --> 00:26:54.249
And a lot of Jewish

00:26:54.250 --> 00:26:56.079
people in the middle of the

00:26:56.080 --> 00:26:58.239
19th century, especially in Germany,

00:26:58.240 --> 00:27:00.249
began to feel

00:27:00.250 --> 00:27:02.079
some sympathy for that, so that

00:27:02.080 --> 00:27:03.939
even when they did not do it

00:27:03.940 --> 00:27:06.309
themselves, as my parents did,

00:27:06.310 --> 00:27:07.310
they

00:27:08.230 --> 00:27:10.959
downplayed any

00:27:10.960 --> 00:27:12.939
part of their heritage

00:27:12.940 --> 00:27:15.339
except one of a strictly

00:27:15.340 --> 00:27:17.599
limited religious cultural sort.

00:27:20.780 --> 00:27:22.459
There are several such exchanges

00:27:22.460 --> 00:27:24.289
where Laurel Vlock is

00:27:24.290 --> 00:27:26.659
pushing Frei to confront

00:27:26.660 --> 00:27:28.459
his identity.

00:27:28.460 --> 00:27:29.869
Towards the end of the interview as

00:27:29.870 --> 00:27:32.389
she confronts him one more time.

00:27:32.390 --> 00:27:33.979
And actually I will end my

00:27:33.980 --> 00:27:35.959
presentation with his words,

00:27:35.960 --> 00:27:37.669
which I think are a good

00:27:37.670 --> 00:27:39.109
introduction to the Q&amp;A.

00:27:43.070 --> 00:27:45.589
This is Laurel Vlock speaking,

00:27:45.590 --> 00:27:47.449
"that takes us back to you and your

00:27:47.450 --> 00:27:49.549
family and the relationship between

00:27:49.550 --> 00:27:51.619
you and your family, which must

00:27:51.620 --> 00:27:53.569
have been, must be or must have been

00:27:53.570 --> 00:27:55.519
strained as a result of your

00:27:55.520 --> 00:27:57.439
departure on your part,

00:27:57.440 --> 00:27:59.509
even though it was clear why

00:27:59.510 --> 00:28:01.039
it happened."

00:28:01.040 --> 00:28:02.389
"My departure from, towards

00:28:02.390 --> 00:28:04.578
Christianity, you mean?".

00:28:04.579 --> 00:28:06.079
"Well, nah, not really towards
Christianty,

00:28:06.080 --> 00:28:07.579
but away from the condition that the

00:28:07.580 --> 00:28:08.882
family found itself in."

00:28:10.369 --> 00:28:12.409
"Actually, no, no. That the problem

00:28:12.410 --> 00:28:14.599
was not that, there.

00:28:14.600 --> 00:28:16.189
The problem was, is not there.

00:28:16.190 --> 00:28:18.049
The problem, I mean they, they

00:28:18.050 --> 00:28:19.759
saw what I was doing as a

00:28:19.760 --> 00:28:21.589
continuation of their own

00:28:21.590 --> 00:28:23.479
pattern, of assimilation on the

00:28:23.480 --> 00:28:25.189
one hand, and moving into an

00:28:25.190 --> 00:28:27.619
academic life on the other hand.

00:28:27.620 --> 00:28:29.449
The problem really for me is that

00:28:29.450 --> 00:28:31.399
I am far more than a good

00:28:31.400 --> 00:28:33.829
many other people at once

00:28:33.830 --> 00:28:36.079
an outsider to Jewishness

00:28:36.080 --> 00:28:37.969
and an insider.

00:28:37.970 --> 00:28:39.439
I find that a very

00:28:40.460 --> 00:28:42.709
difficult way of--"

00:28:42.710 --> 00:28:44.479
unintelligible, it's, it's not clear

00:28:44.480 --> 00:28:45.569
what he says there.

00:28:45.570 --> 00:28:46.819
"I mean, for example, if this

00:28:46.820 --> 00:28:48.259
country were to go officially

00:28:48.260 --> 00:28:49.849
anti-Semitic, which I don't see

00:28:49.850 --> 00:28:52.099
coming, but nonetheless

00:28:52.100 --> 00:28:53.119
it's something like that.

00:28:53.120 --> 00:28:55.339
I would clearly identify myself

00:28:55.340 --> 00:28:56.645
with the Jewish community, but..."

00:28:57.650 --> 00:28:59.689
"Why?" is Vlock

00:28:59.690 --> 00:29:00.979
asking.

00:29:00.980 --> 00:29:02.269
"Well, because I think one should

00:29:02.270 --> 00:29:04.039
always identify with those who are

00:29:04.040 --> 00:29:04.999
persecuted.

00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:06.589
I think that's only right.

00:29:06.590 --> 00:29:09.229
But I think I would do so

00:29:09.230 --> 00:29:11.059
as one whose persuasion

00:29:11.060 --> 00:29:13.009
is one of considerable skepticism

00:29:13.010 --> 00:29:14.419
at the same time.

00:29:14.420 --> 00:29:15.709
There is an author who wrote a

00:29:15.710 --> 00:29:17.639
deeply moving book, Saul

00:29:17.640 --> 00:29:20.029
Friedlander, When Memory Comes,

00:29:20.030 --> 00:29:21.499
have you looked at it?

00:29:21.500 --> 00:29:23.599
And he has become a very loyal,

00:29:23.600 --> 00:29:24.949
devoted Israeli.

00:29:24.950 --> 00:29:27.139
And yet I think I find in that book,

00:29:27.140 --> 00:29:29.160
I found part of the same vein.

00:29:30.500 --> 00:29:32.599
Um, a kind of inability

00:29:32.600 --> 00:29:34.579
to get two halves of

00:29:34.580 --> 00:29:36.589
his personality together again,

00:29:36.590 --> 00:29:39.199
except in a very tenuous way.

00:29:39.200 --> 00:29:41.119
Well, that's true for me,

00:29:41.120 --> 00:29:42.519
too.

00:29:42.520 --> 00:29:44.529
But you see that my dominant

00:29:44.530 --> 00:29:46.509
personality became secular and

00:29:46.510 --> 00:29:47.510
Christian.

00:29:47.740 --> 00:29:50.079
Therefore, it would take a conscious

00:29:50.080 --> 00:29:52.299
move rather than a net,

00:29:52.300 --> 00:29:54.609
natural, emotive response for me

00:29:54.610 --> 00:29:57.219
to identify myself with Judaism

00:29:57.220 --> 00:29:58.089
now.

00:29:58.090 --> 00:30:00.039
I'm too far gone." And

00:30:00.040 --> 00:30:01.089
he smiles.

00:30:01.090 --> 00:30:02.090
Thank you.

00:30:11.423 --> 00:30:12.423
Comments?

00:30:13.650 --> 00:30:14.650
Eva?

00:30:15.220 --> 00:30:16.220
Thank you, both for very clear
[INAUDIBLE]

00:30:17.198 --> 00:30:18.198
Sure.

00:30:19.700 --> 00:30:20.989
Just two points.

00:30:20.990 --> 00:30:22.909
First of all, I

00:30:22.910 --> 00:30:25.429
wonder whether you can see

00:30:25.430 --> 00:30:27.489
the methodology you

00:30:27.490 --> 00:30:29.359
would use in

00:30:29.360 --> 00:30:31.279
the testing on this, because

00:30:31.280 --> 00:30:32.999
[INAUDIBLE] special sources where

00:30:33.000 --> 00:30:34.000
histor- where historians

00:30:35.690 --> 00:30:36.659
[INAUDIBLE] how you can use his

00:30:36.660 --> 00:30:38.539
testimony, which

00:30:38.540 --> 00:30:40.249
[INAUDIBLE] the position of the

00:30:40.250 --> 00:30:42.199
interviewers.

00:30:42.200 --> 00:30:44.449
But we haven't discussed

00:30:44.450 --> 00:30:46.999
yet the structure of the interviews.

00:30:47.000 --> 00:30:48.709
And the second question is connected

00:30:48.710 --> 00:30:49.710
to the first.

00:30:50.830 --> 00:30:51.830
What about

00:30:54.110 --> 00:30:56.009
[INAUDIBLE] stories?

00:30:56.010 --> 00:30:58.249
Because in the first story, this,

00:30:58.250 --> 00:31:00.019
it goes on profession, in the

00:31:00.020 --> 00:31:02.119
profession, and

00:31:03.500 --> 00:31:05.479
in the concentration camp, if it

00:31:05.480 --> 00:31:07.999
had ever happened,

00:31:08.000 --> 00:31:09.829
then once, one can

00:31:09.830 --> 00:31:12.169
keep his or her profession,

00:31:12.170 --> 00:31:14.139
profession, so

00:31:14.140 --> 00:31:15.769
and that may

00:31:16.790 --> 00:31:18.729
continue or discontinue in

00:31:18.730 --> 00:31:20.119
the case of a...

00:31:20.120 --> 00:31:22.039
Is totally different than in the

00:31:22.040 --> 00:31:23.002
case of the [?

00:31:23.003 --> 00:31:25.099
laity ?] because he

00:31:25.100 --> 00:31:27.199
understands, understand

00:31:27.200 --> 00:31:30.069
in the framework of assimilation

00:31:30.070 --> 00:31:31.939
[INAUDIBLE] history of the

00:31:31.940 --> 00:31:34.129
Central European Jews.

00:31:34.130 --> 00:31:35.749
So the question is whether you can

00:31:35.750 --> 00:31:37.729
use the concept of continuity

00:31:37.730 --> 00:31:39.919
and discontinuity and

00:31:39.920 --> 00:31:42.259
in between the

00:31:42.260 --> 00:31:44.149
history between

00:31:44.150 --> 00:31:45.150
that.

00:31:46.090 --> 00:31:47.090
[INAUDIBLE].

00:31:49.310 --> 00:31:50.479
Let's go ahead and take a couple

00:31:50.480 --> 00:31:51.959
more questions, and then, is that

00:31:51.960 --> 00:31:52.974
OK?
Yeah, yes, sure.

00:31:55.850 --> 00:31:57.889
Yes, picking up where Eva left

00:31:57.890 --> 00:31:58.849
off.

00:31:58.850 --> 00:32:01.009
Are you looking into

00:32:01.010 --> 00:32:03.139
how things transpired after

00:32:03.140 --> 00:32:05.389
the war, if, if children were left

00:32:05.390 --> 00:32:08.179
in convents and the parents didn't

00:32:08.180 --> 00:32:10.489
return to pick them up,

00:32:10.490 --> 00:32:12.199
whether the convent kept them,

00:32:12.200 --> 00:32:13.200
whether the convent

00:32:15.170 --> 00:32:17.089
gave them to the Jewish

00:32:17.090 --> 00:32:18.090
community?

00:32:21.430 --> 00:32:23.349
How did things play out at

00:32:23.350 --> 00:32:24.350
the end of the war?

00:32:28.420 --> 00:32:29.420
Take one more question.

00:32:31.040 --> 00:32:32.314
Alright this is both [?

00:32:32.315 --> 00:32:33.289
a fundamental question ?].

00:32:33.290 --> 00:32:34.330
I think, that

00:32:36.210 --> 00:32:38.399
in looking at the statistics,

00:32:38.400 --> 00:32:40.259
that the reason

00:32:40.260 --> 00:32:41.969
that you found so many from

00:32:41.970 --> 00:32:43.949
Czechoslovakia is because we had

00:32:43.950 --> 00:32:46.259
a huge project in Slovakia.

00:32:46.260 --> 00:32:48.539
I think it's not a legitimate

00:32:48.540 --> 00:32:49.540
statistic.

00:32:50.640 --> 00:32:52.559
It has to do with where our

00:32:52.560 --> 00:32:54.659
projects were set up.

00:32:54.660 --> 00:32:56.190
We never taped in Romania.

00:32:57.750 --> 00:32:59.729
We had hundreds

00:32:59.730 --> 00:33:02.279
of tapes done in Czech--,

00:33:02.280 --> 00:33:04.139
in Slovakia, and I

00:33:04.140 --> 00:33:07.079
think it's just that coincidence.

00:33:07.080 --> 00:33:08.939
I'm curious if you saw the

00:33:08.940 --> 00:33:10.123
testimony of Ruth [INAUDIBLE]?

00:33:11.520 --> 00:33:12.520
No.

00:33:12.930 --> 00:33:13.889
Is it in the Fortunoff?

00:33:13.890 --> 00:33:15.749
We have it, we have a sister as

00:33:15.750 --> 00:33:16.200
well.

00:33:16.200 --> 00:33:17.759
All right. Oh.

00:33:17.760 --> 00:33:18.839
Um.

00:33:18.840 --> 00:33:21.689
So this is a case that shows that

00:33:21.690 --> 00:33:23.609
the search itself is not

00:33:23.610 --> 00:33:25.379
comprehensive because I couldn't

00:33:25.380 --> 00:33:26.759
find it.

00:33:26.760 --> 00:33:28.289
So applying the four types of

00:33:28.290 --> 00:33:30.069
search, the name of

00:33:31.300 --> 00:33:32.339
Ruth [INAUDIBLE], it didn't come up

00:33:32.340 --> 00:33:34.108
so, okay, interesting.

00:33:34.109 --> 00:33:35.109
Thanks

00:33:36.360 --> 00:33:37.683
And the other thing is, is the

00:33:37.684 --> 00:33:38.760
male-female dichotomy

00:33:39.990 --> 00:33:41.109
you showed.

00:33:41.110 --> 00:33:43.089
And I think that

00:33:43.090 --> 00:33:44.379
does tell us something.

00:33:44.380 --> 00:33:46.659
I think people were more willing

00:33:46.660 --> 00:33:48.579
to take women, to take girls

00:33:48.580 --> 00:33:50.768
because they weren't circumcised.

00:33:50.769 --> 00:33:51.160
Mm-hmm.

00:33:51.160 --> 00:33:52.989
A boy was immediately

00:33:52.990 --> 00:33:54.849
identifiable and a girl was

00:33:54.850 --> 00:33:56.049
not.

00:33:56.050 --> 00:33:57.789
And I think some of that is a

00:33:57.790 --> 00:33:58.790
function of...

00:34:01.630 --> 00:34:03.669
And I'm, I'm a little puzzled.

00:34:03.670 --> 00:34:05.889
Again, I want to look at the

00:34:05.890 --> 00:34:07.299
records again.

00:34:07.300 --> 00:34:09.339
I know we have at least

00:34:09.340 --> 00:34:10.855
one that I can recall, a Romanian

00:34:12.280 --> 00:34:13.900
little boy who was converted.

00:34:15.250 --> 00:34:17.109
And actually, we edited

00:34:17.110 --> 00:34:19.149
it. It's in our edited testimonies

00:34:19.150 --> 00:34:20.220
and he talks about

00:34:21.440 --> 00:34:23.299
how it bothered him even as

00:34:23.300 --> 00:34:25.579
a little boy, and he said he

00:34:25.580 --> 00:34:27.539
felt that God was going

00:34:27.540 --> 00:34:28.540
to punish him

00:34:30.030 --> 00:34:31.948
because he was converted and Dori

00:34:31.949 --> 00:34:33.809
has a lengthy discussion with

00:34:33.810 --> 00:34:36.049
him about that issue.

00:34:36.050 --> 00:34:38.149
It's Paul D.

00:34:38.150 --> 00:34:39.150
Paul D.

00:34:39.530 --> 00:34:40.530
Yes.

00:34:43.600 --> 00:34:44.518
That's--

00:34:44.519 --> 00:34:46.658
It's possible that, I can't remember

00:34:46.659 --> 00:34:49.299
the geography exactly.

00:34:49.300 --> 00:34:51.011
It may be Ukraine now and not

00:34:51.012 --> 00:34:51.789
Romania.

00:34:51.790 --> 00:34:52.868
Yeah, might be.

00:34:52.869 --> 00:34:54.208
But it was Romania when he was born

00:34:54.209 --> 00:34:56.319
and we usually put down

00:34:56.320 --> 00:34:58.389
as a country

00:34:58.390 --> 00:35:00.339
the name of the country it

00:35:00.340 --> 00:35:01.340
was when they were born.

00:35:02.590 --> 00:35:04.209
I would be really interested to find

00:35:04.210 --> 00:35:05.210
out about this testimony.

00:35:05.490 --> 00:35:07.030
Yeah. Yeah, sure.

00:35:08.160 --> 00:35:10.059
Because it would be great to, to

00:35:10.060 --> 00:35:12.129
finally see a testimony of

00:35:12.130 --> 00:35:13.869
somebody who converted in Romania,

00:35:13.870 --> 00:35:14.870
that would be great. Fantastic.

00:35:19.860 --> 00:35:20.999
Any other questions? You want to
tackle

00:35:21.000 --> 00:35:22.000
the ones--.

00:35:23.909 --> 00:35:24.809
Yeah, yeah, sure. Now, coming to

00:35:24.810 --> 00:35:25.810
Eva's first,

00:35:29.200 --> 00:35:31.139
I know that

00:35:31.140 --> 00:35:33.029
there are a lot of debates about

00:35:33.030 --> 00:35:35.039
the methodology of interviews

00:35:35.040 --> 00:35:36.040
and

00:35:37.080 --> 00:35:39.059
a lot of questions about,

00:35:39.060 --> 00:35:40.439
and especially with the Fortunoff

00:35:40.440 --> 00:35:41.909
Archive at the beginning,

00:35:43.290 --> 00:35:45.929
where there was no specific training

00:35:46.950 --> 00:35:48.879
until they kind of created

00:35:48.880 --> 00:35:51.480
the framework, a structure.

00:35:52.760 --> 00:35:54.649
But at the same time, I like the

00:35:54.650 --> 00:35:56.539
idea of letting the survivor

00:35:56.540 --> 00:35:57.540
talk.

00:35:58.340 --> 00:36:00.019
There are few testimonies I looked

00:36:00.020 --> 00:36:01.999
at when some of them

00:36:02.000 --> 00:36:03.000
were in Serbia.

00:36:04.340 --> 00:36:05.959
There was one in Serbia where the

00:36:05.960 --> 00:36:07.909
interviewer was actually leading

00:36:07.910 --> 00:36:10.229
the, what was leading

00:36:10.230 --> 00:36:12.889
the interview, really.

00:36:12.890 --> 00:36:15.619
So he was asking so many questions

00:36:15.620 --> 00:36:17.659
that it wasn't any more a testimony.

00:36:17.660 --> 00:36:19.760
It was something else.

00:36:20.960 --> 00:36:22.879
But no, the, most of the

00:36:22.880 --> 00:36:24.199
cases I looked at...

00:36:26.780 --> 00:36:28.609
And actually, I had that

00:36:28.610 --> 00:36:30.649
kind of, when I saw

00:36:30.650 --> 00:36:32.509
that, I kind of had a question

00:36:32.510 --> 00:36:34.849
in my mind and I asked myself,

00:36:34.850 --> 00:36:37.099
was there a specific,

00:36:37.100 --> 00:36:38.749
and maybe you could help me here,

00:36:38.750 --> 00:36:39.860
was there a specific

00:36:42.380 --> 00:36:44.459
realization that the

00:36:44.460 --> 00:36:46.849
converts' should be pushed

00:36:46.850 --> 00:36:49.309
with these questions of identity?

00:36:49.310 --> 00:36:51.169
Probably not, because as

00:36:51.170 --> 00:36:52.729
far as I know, the question of

00:36:52.730 --> 00:36:54.619
identity would appear anyway in

00:36:54.620 --> 00:36:56.059
all the testimonies, the way in

00:36:56.060 --> 00:36:58.399
which after the war, the experience

00:36:58.400 --> 00:37:00.559
itself affected

00:37:00.560 --> 00:37:02.759
these people's identity and maybe

00:37:02.760 --> 00:37:03.919
the case of conversion because

00:37:03.920 --> 00:37:05.899
conversion was such a big

00:37:05.900 --> 00:37:07.729
experience.

00:37:07.730 --> 00:37:11.149
Maybe this is why the interviewer

00:37:11.150 --> 00:37:12.979
asked a lot of questions

00:37:12.980 --> 00:37:14.809
and pushed about.

00:37:14.810 --> 00:37:16.489
And how do you feel?

00:37:16.490 --> 00:37:17.329
Do you feel Jewish?

00:37:17.330 --> 00:37:18.559
Do you feel, how do you feel?

00:37:18.560 --> 00:37:20.929
And, um,

00:37:20.930 --> 00:37:22.879
but I think these questions, it's

00:37:22.880 --> 00:37:24.019
great that they are asked.

00:37:25.800 --> 00:37:28.289
Because, um,

00:37:28.290 --> 00:37:29.940
because the survivor is...

00:37:32.030 --> 00:37:34.159
Is giving his or, his or her

00:37:34.160 --> 00:37:36.829
insight into what,

00:37:36.830 --> 00:37:38.449
the way in which that experience

00:37:38.450 --> 00:37:39.450
affected them.

00:37:40.310 --> 00:37:42.659
And the results,

00:37:42.660 --> 00:37:44.899
the answers are sometimes

00:37:44.900 --> 00:37:46.819
extraordinary. You discover

00:37:46.820 --> 00:37:48.709
either feelings of

00:37:48.710 --> 00:37:50.162
embarrassment, shame,

00:37:52.040 --> 00:37:54.019
betrayal, or

00:37:54.020 --> 00:37:55.339
you discover, like in the case of

00:37:55.340 --> 00:37:57.229
Hans Frei and some others,

00:37:57.230 --> 00:37:58.399
he is not the only one.

00:37:58.400 --> 00:38:00.829
I mean, there are a lot of others

00:38:00.830 --> 00:38:03.139
that don't show the same

00:38:04.850 --> 00:38:06.719
trouble by the

00:38:06.720 --> 00:38:07.720
experience.

00:38:08.970 --> 00:38:10.439
But the fact that the interviewer

00:38:10.440 --> 00:38:11.849
asked all those questions

00:38:13.110 --> 00:38:14.110
made this

00:38:15.150 --> 00:38:17.179
kind of clarification possible.

00:38:19.570 --> 00:38:21.760
Continuity and discontinuity,

00:38:23.500 --> 00:38:25.089
yes, and luckily, this is why I

00:38:25.090 --> 00:38:26.090
chose right.

00:38:28.120 --> 00:38:29.590
Because, actually

00:38:31.310 --> 00:38:33.819
I had a kind of dilemma,

00:38:33.820 --> 00:38:35.709
should I pick a testimony that

00:38:35.710 --> 00:38:38.029
is representing

00:38:38.030 --> 00:38:39.949
the majority of the

00:38:39.950 --> 00:38:42.409
converts I found, the testimonies

00:38:42.410 --> 00:38:43.999
of converts I found.

00:38:44.000 --> 00:38:45.739
If, if that was the case, then I

00:38:45.740 --> 00:38:47.629
should have picked up

00:38:47.630 --> 00:38:49.639
a testimony where you have

00:38:49.640 --> 00:38:52.069
this feeling of embarrassment

00:38:52.070 --> 00:38:53.979
and shame and betrayal.

00:38:53.980 --> 00:38:55.039
And there are a lot of these

00:38:55.040 --> 00:38:56.040
testimonies.

00:38:58.180 --> 00:38:59.529
But Frei is different, and I think

00:38:59.530 --> 00:39:00.939
sometimes by looking at the

00:39:00.940 --> 00:39:02.979
different case,

00:39:02.980 --> 00:39:06.009
you can have a

00:39:06.010 --> 00:39:07.059
better sense of,

00:39:08.280 --> 00:39:09.970
um, what is going on.

00:39:11.560 --> 00:39:13.539
So in this case, continuity

00:39:13.540 --> 00:39:15.339
and discontinuity, yes.

00:39:15.340 --> 00:39:17.919
Maybe in Hans Frei's

00:39:17.920 --> 00:39:19.689
cases, this continuity from the

00:39:19.690 --> 00:39:21.190
regular trend.

00:39:24.060 --> 00:39:25.440
Now, coming to your questions,

00:39:28.260 --> 00:39:29.260
I'm,

00:39:30.450 --> 00:39:32.519
I'm basing my kind

00:39:32.520 --> 00:39:34.349
of conclusion on that, what I

00:39:34.350 --> 00:39:36.299
find in the testimonies so I don't

00:39:36.300 --> 00:39:38.409
go, I could go to

00:39:38.410 --> 00:39:40.439
secondary literature about

00:39:40.440 --> 00:39:41.440
what happened with these

00:39:42.900 --> 00:39:45.059
children after

00:39:45.060 --> 00:39:47.009
the war. And I know

00:39:47.010 --> 00:39:49.139
there are a lot of situations where

00:39:49.140 --> 00:39:51.029
children were not returned

00:39:51.030 --> 00:39:52.199
to the relatives.

00:39:53.420 --> 00:39:54.420
Oh,

00:39:55.350 --> 00:39:58.409
yeah, all the situations, but

00:39:58.410 --> 00:40:00.269
based on what I found,

00:40:00.270 --> 00:40:01.619
and there are a lot of testimonies

00:40:01.620 --> 00:40:04.169
from children,

00:40:04.170 --> 00:40:06.209
they are grown adults

00:40:06.210 --> 00:40:08.189
now, who

00:40:08.190 --> 00:40:10.414
were sheltered incumbents.

00:40:11.460 --> 00:40:13.259
There is one very interesting

00:40:13.260 --> 00:40:15.359
testimony, actually.

00:40:15.360 --> 00:40:17.549
There are three testimonies

00:40:17.550 --> 00:40:19.379
of, all of

00:40:19.380 --> 00:40:21.299
them are men, boys.

00:40:21.300 --> 00:40:23.459
They were boys at the time.

00:40:23.460 --> 00:40:25.499
Who found shelter

00:40:25.500 --> 00:40:27.419
in a Belgian

00:40:27.420 --> 00:40:29.519
convent, but

00:40:29.520 --> 00:40:32.339
they didn't know about each other.

00:40:32.340 --> 00:40:33.599
I think they didn't know about each

00:40:33.600 --> 00:40:35.030
other even during the war.

00:40:36.270 --> 00:40:37.270
And then

00:40:38.640 --> 00:40:40.679
after the war,

00:40:40.680 --> 00:40:43.289
there was a call, I think in the US,

00:40:43.290 --> 00:40:45.209
for a, a reunion of all

00:40:45.210 --> 00:40:46.799
the people who found shelter in that

00:40:46.800 --> 00:40:48.749
specific village and

00:40:48.750 --> 00:40:49.889
convent.

00:40:49.890 --> 00:40:51.359
And this is how they met.

00:40:51.360 --> 00:40:53.219
And actually the testimony

00:40:53.220 --> 00:40:54.220
is interesting because

00:40:55.680 --> 00:40:57.869
they are interviewed separately

00:40:57.870 --> 00:40:59.759
and they, then, all of

00:40:59.760 --> 00:41:02.219
them are brought together

00:41:02.220 --> 00:41:03.239
and they are

00:41:04.500 --> 00:41:06.869
kind of discussing,

00:41:06.870 --> 00:41:10.199
joking, and remembering

00:41:10.200 --> 00:41:11.200
the experience

00:41:12.180 --> 00:41:14.070
in that specific context.

00:41:16.110 --> 00:41:19.199
What, what surprises me most

00:41:19.200 --> 00:41:20.200
is

00:41:21.150 --> 00:41:23.129
the fact that this is not

00:41:23.130 --> 00:41:24.130
so...

00:41:24.730 --> 00:41:27.027
The topic of children

00:41:28.280 --> 00:41:30.349
converted in convents

00:41:30.350 --> 00:41:31.920
or Catholic households,

00:41:33.000 --> 00:41:34.000
um,

00:41:35.350 --> 00:41:36.350
is not a myth.

00:41:37.120 --> 00:41:39.159
It's something real and there

00:41:39.160 --> 00:41:40.449
are many testimonies in the

00:41:40.450 --> 00:41:42.429
Fortunoff Archive of such type

00:41:42.430 --> 00:41:43.804
of conversions.

00:41:45.080 --> 00:41:47.049
In some cases you see

00:41:47.050 --> 00:41:48.310
that they...

00:41:49.710 --> 00:41:51.539
They are still attached to that

00:41:51.540 --> 00:41:52.540
experience.

00:41:55.030 --> 00:41:56.822
By the same time, you as a, as an

00:41:58.090 --> 00:42:00.369
observer, you feel

00:42:00.370 --> 00:42:01.370
that

00:42:02.440 --> 00:42:04.869
the experience itself was not right.

00:42:04.870 --> 00:42:06.579
I mean, they were taken advantage

00:42:06.580 --> 00:42:07.580
of.

00:42:09.890 --> 00:42:11.539
They were children not knowing too

00:42:11.540 --> 00:42:13.429
much, but they

00:42:13.430 --> 00:42:15.799
still were persuaded

00:42:15.800 --> 00:42:17.989
in a way or another by families

00:42:17.990 --> 00:42:20.929
or by convents to convert.

00:42:20.930 --> 00:42:23.239
I did not find any situation

00:42:23.240 --> 00:42:24.970
where a child

00:42:27.040 --> 00:42:29.079
or a survivor talks about

00:42:29.080 --> 00:42:30.939
his experience, that he wasn't able

00:42:30.940 --> 00:42:32.979
to return to his family or I

00:42:32.980 --> 00:42:34.949
didn't find such a situation.

00:42:37.090 --> 00:42:38.090
Um.

00:42:41.420 --> 00:42:42.499
Thank you very much for your

00:42:42.500 --> 00:42:44.480
comments, it's, it's great.

00:42:45.500 --> 00:42:47.669
If, if we could find that Romanian,

00:42:47.670 --> 00:42:48.709
that would be, the Romanian

00:42:48.710 --> 00:42:49.869
testimony, that would be great.

00:42:52.220 --> 00:42:54.379
Women, women and

00:42:54.380 --> 00:42:56.539
that the topic of women and

00:42:56.540 --> 00:42:58.489
men, I

00:42:58.490 --> 00:43:00.619
think your your insight is great.

00:43:00.620 --> 00:43:02.119
But at the same time, I should point

00:43:02.120 --> 00:43:03.979
out that, that was a

00:43:03.980 --> 00:43:04.980
trend

00:43:05.990 --> 00:43:08.329
going back 100 and some

00:43:08.330 --> 00:43:09.439
years back,

00:43:10.550 --> 00:43:13.189
of women being more,

00:43:13.190 --> 00:43:15.229
Jewish women converting at

00:43:15.230 --> 00:43:17.329
a higher rate than

00:43:17.330 --> 00:43:18.330
men.

00:43:18.950 --> 00:43:20.779
So that's, that's the,

00:43:20.780 --> 00:43:22.729
all the statistics about conversion

00:43:24.740 --> 00:43:27.019
would show that women converted

00:43:27.020 --> 00:43:28.159
more.

00:43:28.160 --> 00:43:29.329
But there were some other aspects

00:43:29.330 --> 00:43:30.799
that surprised me, I didn't talk

00:43:30.800 --> 00:43:32.719
about all the statistical data here.

00:43:34.610 --> 00:43:36.499
Usually we assume that

00:43:38.030 --> 00:43:40.099
Jews converted in order to

00:43:40.100 --> 00:43:42.259
marry, or for career purposes,

00:43:42.260 --> 00:43:44.269
but I found a lot of testimonies

00:43:44.270 --> 00:43:46.339
mentioning conversions, conversion

00:43:46.340 --> 00:43:47.539
the other way around.

00:43:47.540 --> 00:43:48.540
I mean,

00:43:50.360 --> 00:43:52.429
women converting in order to

00:43:52.430 --> 00:43:54.539
marry a Jewish man.

00:43:54.540 --> 00:43:56.209
There were a lot of such, a lot of

00:43:56.210 --> 00:43:58.399
such cases. I mean, in

00:43:58.400 --> 00:44:00.060
one of the searches, I think for

00:44:00.061 --> 00:44:02.419
baptized, or for

00:44:02.420 --> 00:44:03.420
converted,

00:44:04.880 --> 00:44:06.199
I think there were like forty

00:44:06.200 --> 00:44:07.399
results.

00:44:07.400 --> 00:44:09.199
And almost all of them were about

00:44:09.200 --> 00:44:11.529
this type of, so

00:44:11.530 --> 00:44:14.149
the spouse converted

00:44:14.150 --> 00:44:15.350
to Judaism

00:44:16.910 --> 00:44:17.910
in order to marry.

00:44:22.290 --> 00:44:24.179
OK, one more

00:44:24.180 --> 00:44:25.180
question?

00:44:28.950 --> 00:44:30.599
Because you're dealing with some

00:44:30.600 --> 00:44:32.819
children. Uh, are

00:44:32.820 --> 00:44:34.679
you at a stage where you're able

00:44:34.680 --> 00:44:36.509
to interview people or that's

00:44:36.510 --> 00:44:39.019
not within your,

00:44:39.020 --> 00:44:40.739
your scope?

00:44:40.740 --> 00:44:43.139
Have you spoken to Saul Friedlander,

00:44:43.140 --> 00:44:44.250
for instance?

00:44:46.020 --> 00:44:47.849
No. I must say that

